N. Covert Channels & Tunnelling (DNS, HTTP, ICMP, TLS)

क्या है: data exfil over protocol channels that look normal.
खतरा: DNS tunnelling (TXT/long subdomains), HTTP steganography, TLS covert channels combining encrypted payloads.
Rare/Advanced: multi-protocol staged exfil using low-and-slow timing channels.
Indicators: high entropy in DNS labels, unusual pattern of small requests, long persistent HTTP streams with odd user-agents, JA3 mismatches.
Defense: behavioral detection (Zeek scripts + Suricata), entropy checks, rate limits, egress filtering.
Logs: DNS, http, tls logs; flow records showing long-lived low-volume streams.


