2) हर टॉपिक — पेन-टेस्टिंग POV (क्या होता है, क्यों खतरनाक, indicators, defence)

> हर सेक्शन कॉन्सेप्चुअल है — आपको हमलावर की सोच देता है पर कोई ऑपरेशनल हमला नहीं।



Routing (OSPF / BGP)

क्या ख़तरा: Misconfigured routing or BGP hijacks can redirect traffic globally or locally.

Indicators: Unexpected path changes, AS path anomalies, new next-hops, traceroute discrepancies.

Defence: BGP prefix filtering, RPKI route origin validation, routing change alerts, backup path validation.


NAT / Subnetting

क्या ख़तरा: Poor IP design → broadcast domains too big, overlap, accidental exposure; NAT leakage reveals internal addresses.

Indicators: Unexpected NAT translations, address collisions, private IPs seen externally.

Defence: Clean IP plan, small subnets for security zones, NAT auditing.


Firewalls & ACLs

क्या ख़तरा: Overly-allowing rules, admin mistakes, shadow rules → lateral movement & service exposure.

Indicators: Rare flows through seldom-used rules, last-modified timestamps, rules with 0.0.0.0/0.

Defence: Rule review cadence, least privilege ACLs, policy-as-code and rule test harness.


VPNs & Tunnels

क्या ख़तरा: Misconfigured split-tunnel, weak encryption, weak auth → exfil or backdoor into corp.

Indicators: Persistent long-lived tunnels, unusual remote IPs in tunnel endpoints, tunnel traffic on odd ports.

Defence: Enforce full-tunnel for critical assets, strong algorithms, MFA & cert pinning, monitor tunnel endpoints.


Wireless (WPA2/WPA3, EAP)

क्या ख़तरा: Rogue APs, weak EAP config, enterprise misconfig → client creds capture, mitm.

Indicators: Duplicate SSIDs, AP with same SSID but different BSSID, EAP failures, WPA handshake anomalies.

Defence: 802.1X + EAP-TLS preferred, PMF, management frame protection, enterprise RF surveys, rogue AP detection.


IPv6

क्या ख़तरा: Admins ignore IPv6 → default-enabled, weak firewall rules, SLAAC pitfalls.

Indicators: Unexpected IPv6 traffic, ICMPv6 neighbor anomalies.

Defence: Explicit IPv6 policy, RA guard, firewall rules for v6, log IPv6 flows.


BGP threats

क्या ख़तरा: Prefix hijack leads to massive eavesdrop/DoS; especially dangerous for cloud/peering.

Indicators: Sudden routing shifts, BGP origin change, traffic blackholing.

Defence: Filtering, RPKI, monitoring services, AS path sanity checks.


Cloud Networking (VPCs)

क्या ख़तरा: Misconfigured SGs/NACLs, open metadata endpoints, public S3, cross-account roles.

Indicators: New public endpoints, unusual IAM role usage, long-lived public ports.

Defence: least privilege IAM, VPC flow logs, cloud-native IDS, block metadata where not needed.


OT/ICS Networking

क्या ख़तरा: Legacy protocols with no auth (Modbus, DNP3). Air-gap myths.

Indicators: Unexpected traffic on ICS ports, engineering workstations bridging IT/OT.

Defence: Strong segmentation (physically), protocol gateways, asset inventory, vendor patch policy.


Application Proxies & APIs

क्या ख़तरा: Auth bypass via misconfigured proxy, token leakage, weak rate limits → API abuse.

Indicators: Bursts of API requests, expired tokens used, unusual endpoints.

Defence: API gateways, auth scopes, WAF, proper logging.



---

3) Advanced / Rare लेकिन जानना ज़रूरी (Industry surprises) ⚠️

Layer-2 forwarding plane exploits: CAM overflow (flooding) to force switch into “hub” mode.

Split-brain routing via BGP misconfig + cloud peering — attacker triggers route blackhole by manipulating transit.

Metadata exfil via cloud instance (IMDS v1 vs v2 issues) — cloud-specific high-impact leak.

Side-channel EM/TEMPEST on copper runs — rare, but targeted attackers use it for high-value targets.

Firmware supply-chain compromise — baseline firmware hashes and code signing checks are critical.



