5) Penetration-Test Track — पूरा सीखने/प्रैक्टिस ट्रैक (0 → Pro) 🎓🛠️

Stage 0 — Foundations (0–4 weeks)

Networking basics: OSI, TCP/IP, ARP, switching, routing, subnetting.

Practical: build mini lab, basic packet captures (Wireshark) — analysis only.


Stage 1 — Visibility & Detection (4–12 weeks)

Zeek logs parsing, NetFlow analysis, SIEM basics, writing simple detection rules.

Practice: baseline traffic, create anomalies in lab, detect them.


Stage 2 — Defensive Hardening & Purple Teaming (3–6 months)

Configure port-security, DHCP snooping, BGP filtering, firewall policies.

Build detection playbooks and test with red-team in isolated lab.


Stage 3 — Offensive Theory & Labs (6–12 months)

Deep dive into protocol weaknesses conceptually (ARP/DHCP/DNS/SMB).

Hands-on in authorized CTFs / labs (TryHackMe, HTB, OffSec). Focus on detection evasion theory and defenses.


Stage 4 — Specialist Paths (ongoing)

Network attack surface specialist: BGP, MPLS, carrier-grade.

Cloud network specialist: VPCs, cloud-native IDS, IAM networking.

OT/ICS specialist: industrial protocols, safety-first testing.


Certifications to target (suggested)

Network+/Security+ → foundation

OSCP / eJPT / PEN-200 (OffSec) → practical offensive skills (lab only)

GCIA/GCIH/GRE (SANS) → detection/incident response mastery

CCNA/CCNP (networking depth) and cloud certs (AWS/GCP Cloud Security) for cloud networking.



