11) “जो आप नहीं जानते होगा” — Hidden nuggets (short, punchy) 💣

Cloud metadata (IMDS v1 vs v2) loopholes are one of the fastest ways to steal keys from instances.

IPv6 is often left unmonitored and becomes an easy bypass for IPv4-only controls.

BGP misconfig on a single peer can route your traffic through a hostile AS for minutes — monitoring + RPKI matters.

Firmware-level implants are stealthy: asset procurement and firmware hash baselines are defense essentials.

OT networks often fail basic logging; absence of logs = huge blindspot.



